    {
      "id": 479496,
      "username": "SanaullaHaq",
      "name": "Sanaulla Haq",
      "created_at": "2025-08-31T06:13:17.762Z",
      "cooked": "<p>What we have done is given below. Though this is not perfect, but it works. This implementaion does not require any change in the core frappe code.</p>\n<p>I call the <code>disable_prepared_report_being_checked()</code> before <code>return columns, data</code> statment in the <code>script_report.py</code> file.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">def disable_prepared_report_being_checked(report_name):\n    \"\"\"\n    Uncheck the prepared_report checkbox and remove `Prepared Report` entity (if any)\n    \"\"\"\n    frappe.db.set_value('Report', report_name, 'prepared_report', 0)\n    # frappe.db.delete('Prepared Report')               # Truncates the entire table\n    frappe.db.delete('Prepared Report', {'report_name': report_name})\n    frappe.db.commit()\n</code></pre>\n<p>This code unchecks the <code>Prepared Report</code> check box everytime it executes and deletes the prepared report entity from <code>Prepared Report</code> table (if any).</p>",
